\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Overall workflow of the proposed TL-QLDMR model. Normal-weather source samples and scarce extreme-weather target samples are first organized as cross-domain inputs, then processed through supervised transfer adaptation with shared kernel representation, MMD-based feature alignment, and weighted label learning. These components are integrated into a quantile-aware LDMR objective and optimized either by exact dual quadratic programming or by the scalable Nystr\"om + mini-batch SGD solver, yielding both point forecasts and probabilistic prediction intervals.}}{6}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:framework}{{1}{6}{Overall workflow of the proposed TL-QLDMR model. Normal-weather source samples and scarce extreme-weather target samples are first organized as cross-domain inputs, then processed through supervised transfer adaptation with shared kernel representation, MMD-based feature alignment, and weighted label learning. These components are integrated into a quantile-aware LDMR objective and optimized either by exact dual quadratic programming or by the scalable Nystr\"om + mini-batch SGD solver, yielding both point forecasts and probabilistic prediction intervals}{figure.caption.1}{}}
